  "purpose": "Replace the empty western pasture shoulder with small golden crop beds, native stake divisions and a worked-soil headland leading to a useful garden grower. Preserve the complete 30x22 early route, both actual town roads, existing original ledge and fenced drain, both full native buildings and their room returns. Existing original Minnesota trainers/encounters and story programs are authoritative; do not rebuild from the stale Johto parties in the historical R02 dossier.",
  "status": "Unselected source proposal; native publication, new reward dispatch and production traversal/capacity/Continue remain required.",
  "review_corrections": [
    "v01 made an overly broad bare-soil apron. v02 replaces five of those cells with native golden crops, leaving the two-tile working approach and the grower turnout. The original long route and first-badge services retain their exact approaches and grass costs."
  ]
